{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere","id":1058573,"title":"Human organs creation using Life sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-05T14:33:23-08:00","id":1058573,"title":"Human organs creation using Life sphere","content":"I'm trying to develop a concept of a low-power enlightened doctor that somehow synthetizes artificial human organs for transplant. Using M20 corebook and HDYDT books, I know that with Life 4 it is possible to create such organ and implant it into the patient, using the medical equipment and the surgery as a focus.<br /> <br /> But, If said character were to do something simpler, like, say, transform raw meat into a temporarily transplantable organ, and perfoming the surgery by mundane means, which spheres should he use? My best guess is matter 2 (for the raw meat) to life 3 (medium complexity for creating a human organ). What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:36:41-08:00","id":1058785,"title":"","content":"Matter 2, Life 3, Prime 2 (perhaps Time?)<br /> <br /> you are trying to revive Life function of something that has undergone Cell Death, You need Matter to anchor the initial effects to the base meterial you may need a Time Effect thrown in to transform the dead flesh to it's pre-Cell Death state, then a Life effect to make the Meat in to a compatible organ and Prime to sustain the effects until the organ can be integrated in to the recipients Pattern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:12:20-08:00","id":1058834,"title":"","content":"Matter 2 / Life 3 sounds good to me, too. Time shouldn't be needed, although Prime 2 doesn't hurt to vitalize the matter.<br /> After that just preserve and transplant the old fashioned way.<br /> <br /> BONUS:<br /> You might be able to use Life 3 to also analyze the organ inside the patient, so the meat gets transformed into a virtual clone of the patient's organ, just in a healthy state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:34:26-08:00","id":1058861,"title":"","content":"To add, this whole shebang can actually be pulled off in a Coincidental way. We live in a time where we have started to actually 3D print living tissue for transplants in RL, so if said Mage works with a similiar (but of course much improved!) setup, nobody will think that something is..off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:03:54-08:00","id":1058870,"title":"","content":"Well... The easiest way would be to produce those in ANOTHER living being. That would still technically be Life 4... But if we consider that an organ is a &quot;simpler lifeform&quot; than a fully grown human being, than yeah, we could adapt it for those limited uses to be in the spectrum of Life 2/3 (so, those tribal Shamans that shrink the heads of their fallen enemies, could do it with Life 2 only).<br /> <br /> This kind of procedure can be VERY powerful, because lets the Mage do things he couldn't... At least in theory.<br /> <br /> Remember to make all those organs permanent (unless you wanna a heart that you've grown from lettuce to returning to its vegetal state. Inside the host. While this may sound terrible, it can, in fact, be quite useful. Make those corporates your slaves by requiring constant upkeep on their &quot;miraculous hearts&quot;)<br /> <br /> Besides that, you'll also need anti rejection drugs. Simple drugs for &quot;normal&quot; organs, that just do whatever a common organ do, but if your &quot;super enhanced heart&quot; gives you +1 Stamina cardio bonus, or muscle with +1 Strenght, lungs that can remain under water for an hour and things like that, you'll need special &quot;hiperscience&quot; drugs or alchemical compounds. Over time however, those transplants take their toll over the health of the patient.<br /> <br /> I've been just thinking, Matter 4/Life 3 is all you need to get those cool Cyber augments, but if you wanna reliable cybers without all those side effects (permadox and genetic flaws are enough), you should go for the Life 4 version","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:16:18-08:00","id":1058910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058870#post1058870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides that, you'll also need anti rejection drugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why I suggested using Life 3 to also analyze the heart of the patient - so the heart created out of the meat won't get rejected, as it essentially is their own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:45:08-08:00","id":1058953,"title":"","content":"I think you will need Life 4:<br /> <br /> At this Rank, the mage may enact radical changes on any complex<br /> organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth. He can uplift other<br /> species with new limbs, opposable thumbs, increased brain capacity,<br /> etc., so long as he doesn\u2019t change their intrinsic nature.<br /> <br /> Because Life 3 only works on simple organisms and I doubt that StoryTellers would let you get away with saying that an organ is a simple lifeform:<br /> <br /> Advanced understanding allows the mage to radically<br /> alter simple organisms (turning a tree inside-out); transform<br /> one into another (changing fruit into insects); or \u2013 with Prime 2 \u2013 conjure<br /> them from raw energy.<br /> <br /> Quotes from M20 pp516-517, YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:55:56-08:00","id":1058958,"title":"","content":"However, you can heal complex organisms with Life 3, soo..<br /> Yeah, I think it's a thing that might be quite up to the ST in this case I think, wether separately growing/cloning a single organ constitutes a complex organism effect or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:58:33-08:00","id":1058959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058910#post1058910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly why I suggested using Life 3 to also analyze the heart of the patient - so the heart created out of the meat won't get rejected, as it essentially is their own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, lets think it over a little bit.<br /> <br /> Lets say, for example, that the patient's heart have a genetic flaw that makes it somehow flawed, which could cause a series of problems (well, that would be the reason to need a transplant in the first place).<br /> <br /> Some times, you can correct the problem with a &quot;simple&quot; cirurgy.<br /> <br /> If thats the case, there is no reason to grown a new heart, you can just open the person, use Life 3 in his own heart, and put it back in place.<br /> <br /> Yes, you could of course grown a new one in a tube, and make the correction on it.<br /> <br /> If, however, it is something a cirurgy can't fix, and a transplant is needed, things get messed.<br /> <br /> You can grow a new heart, with just some minor genetic alterations, to make the new heart healthy.<br /> <br /> Thing is, when you alter its DNA, it will get rejected by the body.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that, if you change somebody eyes to be as good as the eyes of an eagle, thats surely going to cause rejection.<br /> <br /> Thats all from a scientific viewpoint of course, but you can generalize it for any mystical views either... &quot;The growth organs cause rejection because they aren't born by the same animating life force&quot;, or &quot;their humurous aren't EXACTLY the same, even thou they are very close&quot;, and so on.<br /> <br /> All that is also a good excuse to say &quot;To make organs with fiiting DNA, or with connected life force or with the same humurous fluids, you need Life 4&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:03:22-08:00","id":1058963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058953#post1058953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you will need Life 4:<br /> <br /> At this Rank, the mage may enact radical changes on any complex<br /> organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth. He can uplift other<br /> species with new limbs, opposable thumbs, increased brain capacity,<br /> etc., so long as he doesn\u2019t change their intrinsic nature.<br /> <br /> Because Life 3 only works on simple organisms and I doubt that StoryTellers would let you get away with saying that an organ is a simple lifeform:<br /> <br /> Advanced understanding allows the mage to radically<br /> alter simple organisms (turning a tree inside-out); transform<br /> one into another (changing fruit into insects); or \u2013 with Prime 2 \u2013 conjure<br /> them from raw energy.<br /> <br /> Quotes from M20 pp516-517, YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, RAW it would be it.<br /> <br /> What we are discussing here would fall much more under house rules or headcannon, or at must, interpretation of cannon.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it would depend totally on if the ST would consider separated organs as &quot;simple life&quot; or not (well, a human liver is &quot;simpler&quot; than a shrimp from a biochemical viewpoint)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:10:46-08:00","id":1058966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058958#post1058958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, you can heal complex organisms with Life 3, soo..<br /> Yeah, I think it's a thing that might be quite up to the ST in this case I think, wether separately growing/cloning a single organ constitutes a complex organism effect or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never like that whole Life 2/3 for heal... Specially, I hate that rule of self heal being easier than healing others, it makes absolutely no sense at all.<br /> <br /> To me, the only reason for that is for game balance (requiring Life 4 to start healing would be too tough on players), not real mechanics logic.<br /> <br /> And I also dont like that you need one extra level to do on others what you can do to yourself, it also doesn't make sense. You should be able to give claws to someone with Life 3, as well as you should be able to turn frogs into dragons with Life 5 (not just ridiculously small ones).<br /> <br /> That again, looks like just another game balance done, that doesn't really make any sense.<br /> <br /> So, in my own house rules, I set ANY healing or Life damage (to complex organisms, for invertabrates and non animals is Life 2) as Life 3, and I make all the effects that you can use on yourself, usable on others (so, those modifications I make it to be Life 3 anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:14:00-08:00","id":1058970,"title":"","content":"Yes. Healing a patient using some sort of special organ adaptation, cleaning any genetic flaw, etc is Life 4, as stated in M20. Removing small genetic flaws is Life 3 if we believe Progenitors revised (basically, an inversion of the Destructive Genegineering procedure).<br /> <br /> My idea is, to create externally a rather generic organ, compatible with the patient, and then transplant it using mundane medicine (with anti-rejection drugs and immunosupressants). Of course, such effect might even be temporary, but that's part of the idea (insert evil laughter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:18:50-08:00","id":1058975,"title":"","content":"&gt;Like I said, it would depend totally on if the ST would consider separated organs as &quot;simple life&quot; or not (well, a human liver is &quot;simpler&quot; than a shrimp from a biochemical viewpoint)<br /> Not from a DNA point of view though - although then we are getting into a science paradigm...<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact whether an organism is simple or complex probably depends a <b>lot </b>on your paradigm/belief system.<br /> <br /> For science based tech paradigms you would have to start considering the tree of life, evolution, and size/complexity of DNA and chromosomes. Which means that birds could be considered the same as humans.<br /> <br /> Whereas with a more 'pimitive'* belief system all animals could be considered 'simpler' than humans.<br /> <br /> *I can't think of a better word to describe the opposite of scientific","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 03-06-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:54:02-08:00","id":1058991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058975#post1058975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not from a DNA point of view though - although then we are getting into a science paradigm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thats where you're mistaken... You'd be surprised my friend...<br /> <br /> This idea of &quot;evolution&quot; is a XIX century idea. The concept of &quot;evolution&quot; (as in, betterment, basically, the idea that life came from simple forms, and it got successive improvements, until reaching the Human form, the apex of evolutionary complexity).<br /> The XXI century &quot;theory of evolution&quot; sees it as CHANGE. The organisms dont IMPROVE, they just <i>change</i> over time.<br /> You know, there are plants with more complex DNA than us.<br /> Many apes have more chromossomes than us.<br /> DNA aint all that matters for complexity or not, also, it ISNT DNA alone, despite popular belief, that determines the living being. Organisms are a complex interaction; the same gene can get <u>different interaction</u> under differently situations, which means, the same DNA sequences can produce <u>different results</u> (for example, a gene can produce Protein A under the enzim X, but the same gene will instead produce Protein B if it is under the influence of enzim Y. So, if the mother of a baby only produces enzim Y, that baby will only have Protein B, even if he have the gene to produce Protein A).<br /> Thats why the Genome Project failed; simply knowing DNA sequences is useless, you need to know all the biochemestry of a being to know how that biochemestry will activate or surpresa its genetic expression (in the example I gave - maybe, under an excessive amount of Protein B, another unrelated gene, the gene that produces the enzime Y is supressed, and the gene that produces enzime X activated, so, after the cell producing too much Protein B, another pair of genes would interfere, making THE SAME GENE start to produce Protein A once again... And the same process would occur, after too much production of the Protein A.<br /> Now, try to imagine this same process working for hundreds of thousands of different genes, which can have different expressions under some millions of different proteins, sugars, oils, inorganic components and many many other kinds of biochemical components.<br /> Thats why you would need a quantum computer to predict all those interactions - well, maybe thats not a problem for technocrats)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:04:44-08:00","id":1058995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1058975#post1058975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not from a DNA point of view though - although then we are getting into a science paradigm...<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact whether an organism is simple or complex probably depends a <b>lot </b>on your paradigm/belief system.<br /> <br /> For science based tech paradigms you would have to start considering the tree of life, evolution, and size/complexity of DNA and chromosomes. Which means that birds could be considered the same as humans.<br /> <br /> Whereas with a more 'pimitive'* belief system all animals could be considered 'simpler' than humans.<br /> <br /> *I can't think of a better word to describe the opposite of scientific</div> </div> </div> </div>We can't mix &quot;Paradigm&quot; with &quot;Game Mechanics&quot;. Grass can be more complex, from a biochemichal viewpoint, than a shark.<br /> <br /> Those matters ARENT a matter of &quot;scientific accuracy&quot; or even of Paradigm, but rather, a matter of <u>game balance</u> and practical rules.<br /> <br /> You dont give a &quot;better Spirit Sphere&quot; to Dreamspeakers because &quot;uh, they are so badassess with spirits&quot;. No, you use THE SAME spirit Sphere, but they can make different uses of it than a VE with Dimensional Science, for example.<br /> <br /> Same Sphere, different uses.<br /> <br /> Same mechanics, different applications under Paradigms.<br /> <br /> That differentiation of &quot;simple&quot; and &quot;complex&quot; life as vertebrates and anything-else is NOT a scientific division. But, it fullfills the purposes of the game mechanics - and it is good for Technocrats or Verbena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:21:55-08:00","id":1059007,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, what are the upper limits of &quot;Simple&quot; Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:09:51-08:00","id":1059056,"title":"","content":"<b>Paradigms <i>are </i>game mechanics!</b><br /> <br /> Some paradigms do get a worse Sphere for certain effects. I can't find it right now but there's at least one mystic healing paradigm that has much higher Sphere requirements than the standard charts. So in theory the Sphere rank for a specific effect is not necessarily the same for all paradigms - generally it will be but not absolutely in all cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:13:27-08:00","id":1059150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059056#post1059056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Paradigms <i>are </i>game mechanics!</b><br /> <br /> Some paradigms do get a worse Sphere for certain effects. I can't find it right now but there's at least one mystic healing paradigm that has much higher Sphere requirements than the standard charts. So in theory the Sphere rank for a specific effect is not necessarily the same for all paradigms - generally it will be but not absolutely in all cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. It is the same spheres for ALL Paradigms.<br /> <br /> This is NOT Dark Ages Mage, where each Paradigm would have its own set of Spheres. The game mechanics for Spheres are the same for all.<br /> <br /> What the Paradigm can change is <b>how you use the Spheres</b> (aside from the foci to use them). Paradigm is NOT just game mechanics, its about Roleplaying, first and foremost.<br /> <br /> The Sphere system is a game mechanic that exists at the level of the players; its NOT an attribute intrinsic to the game world (you'll never hear an Hermetic saying &quot;oh, I'll get him a Life 3 heal and its all good&quot;).<br /> <br /> The Paradigm however, is part of the scenario, of the fluff of the game. An Etherite will NEVER say &quot;Let me Life 3 him to his feet&quot;. But, he WILL say &quot;oh, I have just saw the new publication of the <b>Paradigm</b> magazine giving very interesting details about molecular healing with X-Rays... I'll take my cosmic condensator and you'll be back on your feet in a second!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Resume: the Spheres levels are invisible in the game level, being only a rule system for the players; Paradigm however, is built in the world scenario.<br /> <br /> What you're saying would be the same as saying that the Brawl talent should work differently for each character, or Drive, or that Willpower should have different rules for men and women or christians, buddhists and atheists.<br /> <br /> Like attributes, abilities and willpower, Spheres are part of the game rules, therefore, they are universal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:15:35-08:00","id":1059151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059007#post1059007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, what are the upper limits of &amp;quot;Simple&amp;quot; Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that isn't a Vertebrate (plants, bacteria, fungus, worms, insects, spiders, octopuses... But anything from fishes to apes like us is Life 4/5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:40:41-08:00","id":1059358,"title":"","content":"Thanks. So, what would it take to transform an invertebrate into a fully functioning organ? And what about pattern bleeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:49:20-08:00","id":1059424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059358#post1059358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. So, what would it take to transform an invertebrate into a fully functioning organ? And what about pattern bleeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, turning a octopus into a human heart? In theory, it would be Life 5.<br /> <br /> And, there is no pattern bleeding if you make changes permanent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T05:01:24-08:00","id":1059440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059151#post1059151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything that isn't a Vertebrate (plants, bacteria, fungus, worms, insects, spiders, octopuses... But anything from fishes to apes like us is Life 4/5)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've often seen people include amphibians and even lizards in simple life forms. M20 seems to have left that up in the air (or maybe I'm not looking at the final copy) because it doesn't mention either of them. Given the position of frogs in folklore it feels right that they should be simple life forms, but I don't think it matters too much, overall.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to get into the scientific weeds, the best threshold would probably be diploblasts vs. triploblasts, but that's hell of a conversation to get into for game mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:18:07-08:00","id":1059486,"title":"","content":"If you're going only by M20, this is all it seems to say:<br /> Simple organisms \u2013 viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc.<br /> complex organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth.<br /> <br /> Earlier versions set the line between vertebrates &amp; invertebrates it seems<br /> <br /> Are there any other distinct divisions that fit between the above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-07-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:33:49-08:00","id":1059495,"title":"","content":"Chordates vs non-chordates (spines vs no spines).<br /> <br /> Quadroblasts vs Triploblasts (chordate neural crest vs other neural structures, pretty much the same as above. Also, the argument that chordates are quadroblasts is not universal).<br /> <br /> Warm blooded vs cold/non blooded.<br /> <br /> Hard eggshells and other methods for controlling the environment of embryos. (Really, really sketchy because it is up in the air what counts. This one would have fish and amphibians as simple while creatures with hard eggshells, creatures that give live birth, and creatures that hatch eggs internally (sharks) would be complex.)<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of for now.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:58:41-08:00","id":1059512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059495#post1059495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chordates vs non-chordates (spines vs no spines).<br /> <br /> Quadroblasts vs Triploblasts (chordate neural crest vs other neural structures, pretty much the same as above. Also, the argument that chordates are quadroblasts is not universal).<br /> <br /> Warm blooded vs cold/non blooded.<br /> <br /> Hard eggshells and other methods for controlling the environment of embryos. (Really, really sketchy because it is up in the air what counts. This one would have fish and amphibians as simple while creatures with hard eggshells, creatures that give live birth, and creatures that hatch eggs internally (sharks) would be complex.)<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of for now.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:26:21-08:00","id":1059569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059486#post1059486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going only by M20, this is all it seems to say:<br /> Simple organisms \u2013 viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc.<br /> complex organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth.<br /> <br /> Earlier versions set the line between vertebrates &amp; invertebrates it seems</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe main result of this change, I found, was that it is no longer feasible to make it rain colossal squid using Life 3/Prime 2. I am undecided on whether this is a good thing or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:27:52-08:00","id":1059598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059486#post1059486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going only by M20, this is all it seems to say:<br /> Simple organisms \u2013 viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc.<br /> complex organism \u2013 people, dogs, horses, and so forth.<br /> <br /> Earlier versions set the line between vertebrates &amp; invertebrates it seems<br /> <br /> Are there any other distinct divisions that fit between the above?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Im still getting the feel of my beautiful, aromatic, platonic, sublime, and brand new M20... Im living it. ALMOST perfect. Almost.<br /> <br /> The book has several improvements overall on MANY rules, I loved all its charts for magik, I'll be adopting most of its changes (with a few exceptions)<br /> <br /> But the Spheres descriptions SUCKS ON A COSMIC LEVEL. My dear god, Im luck I hadn't have to learn Mage by M20, because it would've been A FREAKING MESS. I heard some guys here saying that they never had contact with the previous versions... For any of those out there, how can you play the game AT ALL?<br /> <br /> And, from what I heard of it, I WONT get that &quot;How Do You Do That?&quot;. No way on Earth will I agree that Prime 2 is a <u>mandatory</u> sphere for akashics or other stupid things like that which I heard people talking about.<br /> <br /> So... Yes, the description on M20 about &quot;complex&quot; and &quot;simple&quot; life is VERY vague.<br /> Just as is its ENTIRE Spheres description (huge con M20, shame on you).<br /> <br /> Other than that MAJOR flaw, Im loving the book, and Im loving most of the changes (I dont like HAP and all that nonsense about conjuring taxis, but thats all minor adjusts)<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, I forgot, yeah, Revised puts this line as Vertebrate/Invertebrate.<br /> <br /> I liked that whole thing of frogs that Ramnses said thou, and since frogs aren't exactly killing machines (althouth Im pretty sure my etherite can fix that), so I guess its ok to put them in that category... Ok, thats the line I'll adopt from now on, reptiles, birds and mammals - complex. All else, simple. Thanks Ramnesis!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","user":"AgentSmith","date":". 03-07-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:49:53-08:00","id":1059607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059569#post1059569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe main result of this change, I found, was that it is no longer feasible to make it rain colossal squid using Life 3/Prime 2. I am undecided on whether this is a good thing or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Squid is a mollusk, so you can still make the &quot;giant squid rain&quot; 11th plague of Egypt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T06:08:58-08:00","id":1060047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059598#post1059598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard some guys here saying that they never had contact with the previous versions... For any of those out there, how can you play the game AT ALL?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Differently.<br /> <br /> I'm introducing the game to people who've never used the previous versions. Apparently, if you go solely by the descriptions in M20, it's more flexible at some points than previous versions. At others it forces the storyteller to make (often arbitrary) decisions about the setting they are running. The upper or lower boundaries of simple life, for example, which seems at this point that it can be as low as invertebrate to vertebrate or as high as non-mammals to mammals. In some ways, it's a bit like first edition all over again. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1059598#post1059598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, from what I heard of it, I WONT get that &quot;How Do You Do That?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found that book almost useless (I liked one or two parts at least) and sold it for really cheap at the first opportunity. (Sorry authors)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:22:03-08:00","id":1060098,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's not easy to define biological complexity in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:37:46-08:00","id":1060107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058573-human-organs-creation-using-life-sphere?p=1060098#post1060098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it's not easy to define biological complexity in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. On the one hand you have invertebrates as supposedly not complex... then you have things like octopi which are pretty complex in their own way. Then there's the mantis shrimp that looks like some sort of mage experiment that got free and started breeding in the wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}